profile: tinyrustlm-mirust.llms-full-export.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-08-28T20:20:00Z
canonical_public_source: /llms-full.txt

product_contract:
  - TinyRustLM is one clean-slate prelaunch browser-local product.
  - A current composition is exactly model.slm2, tokenizer.tokenizer2, template.template2, sampling.sampling2, prompt.prompt2, and composition.acg2.
  - There is no legacy reader, compatibility alias, migration, fallback, response repair, hidden retry, best-of-N, or accepted debt.
  - Project sites do not receive prompts or model bytes; model bytes remain local or move directly between consenting peers.

package_contract:
  - The default public package transaction is exactly TinyRustLM.Abstractions, TinyRustLM.Core, and TinyRustLM.P2P.
  - TinyRustLM.MemoryEndpoints is separately optional, excluded from the default transaction, and does not become model-byte transport.

memory_endpoints_two_uses:
  - Direct agent lane: agents across every maintained ecosystem site use MemoryEndpoints.com for agent-to-agent long-term memory, meetings, handoffs, and coordination.
  - User plugin lane: a TinyRustLM.com Connect user signs in to MemoryEndpoints.com and explicitly selects it as TinyRustLM.com Connect long-term memory.
  - Keep identity, credentials, consent, scopes, provenance, idempotency, and receipts separate; neither lane silently acts for the other.
  - Authorization, implementation, configuration, fixtures, mocks, or reachability do not prove a live operation.

prelaunch_redundancy:
  - Important memory may also be kept in current .uai, wiki, public-safe source notes, and approved private stores.
  - Keep every maintained copy current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory; surface and reconcile conflicts.

evidence_and_history:
  - Historical runtime documents are retained only as clearly labeled immutable evidence and have no current compatibility authority.
  - The Qwen3 attempt /10 remains terminal failure and cannot be rerun, repaired, adopted, promoted, deleted, or reinterpreted.
  - Campaign counters remain 0/20 qualified models, 0/50 clean browser rounds, 0/25 live memory rounds, 0/40 externally proven P2P lanes, and 0/20 catalog announcements until exact receipts exist.
